StreamPredictor::getNextLine() reads each row into a temporary int array of
rowBytes - pixBytes entries, four times the row size. /Columns can make a
row ~256 MB (the constructor only guards rowBytes against int overflow), so
a stream of a few bytes asks for a 1 GB array per row: a bad_alloc abort on
the 512 MB wasm heap. The constructor allocates predLine (rowBytes) with
gmalloc(), which aborts when that fails.

Read the raw row in chunks of at most 4096 ints, so the temporary stays
16 KB; the bytes and the EOF handling are unchanged (getRawChars() fills
EOF past the end, and the loop stops at the first EOF as before). Allocate
predLine with gmalloc_checkoverflow() and leave the predictor not ok when
it fails, which the Flate/LZW streams already handle. Regression test
cpp/tests/poppler-predictor-row-test.cpp fails every operator new above
256 MB and checks PNG Sub/Up rows that span several chunks.

Not fixed upstream as of d50f45b.
Upstream: related open MR !2404 (StreamPredictor: fix negative-shift UB and
16-bit truncation in TIFF predictor, 2026-10-18) touches the same function's
TIFF part, not this allocation; none found for the row allocation.

